0,"conf":"high","t":"heading","path":[]},{"status":"same","key":"legend-1","old_key":"legend-1","old_version":"2024.1B","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"note","path":["s-legend"]},{"status":"changed","key":"legend-4","old_key":"legend-2","old_version":"2024.1B","sim":0.966,"conf":"medium","t":"note","path":["s-legend"],"moved":true,"diff":[["-","[2]"],["+","[4]"],["=","The points required for moving up (or down) is based on the points in the dancer’s primary role, not the combined points in their primary and secondary roles."]]},{"status":"changed","key":"legend-6","old_key":"legend-4","old_version":"2024.1B","sim":0.975,"conf":"medium","t":"note","path":["s-legend"],"moved":true,"diff":[["-","[4]"],["+","[6]"],["=","Newcomer division is not offered at all events. Competitors may select either Newcomer or Novice divisions, but must dance in Novice once they receive one (1) point in either Newcomer OR Novice in their selected role (primary or secondary)."]]},{"status":"changed","key":"legend-7","old_key":"legend-5","old_version":"2024.1B","sim":0.982,"conf":"medium","t":"note","path":["s-legend"],"moved":true,"diff":[["-","[5]"],["+","[7]"],["=","Registry Events are allowed to waive a competition round if the number of competitors is no more than 10% over the previous Tier’s maximum (e.g., a Tier 4 contest with 43 Followers (and fewer than 39 Leaders) could run a prelims and finals only). This is allowed to provide stability for contest planning."]]},{"status":"changed","key":"legend-8","old_key":"legend-6","old_version":"2024.1B","sim":0.889,"conf":"medium","t":"note","path":["s-legend"],"moved":true,"diff":[["-","[6]"],["+","[8]"],["=","“Numerical” added for clarity, effective March 27, 2024."]]},{"status":"removed","old_key":"3.2.5a-i","old_version":"2024.1B","t":"item","path":["3","3.2"],"text":"Competitors who do not meet the Registry Event’s qualifications for Champions or All Stars, even if they have Champion points, must submit a petition and receive approval to dance in the appropriate division."},{"status":"removed","old_key":"3.2.10","old_version":"2024.1B","t":"item","path":["3","3.2"],"text":"Registry Events must allow competitors who have a minimum of 150 All Star points or 10 Champion points to compete in a WSDC Champion Jack & Jill contest, if offered at the event. Competitors who qualify are not required to compete in Champions."},{"status":"removed","old_key":"legend-3","old_version":"2024.1B","t":"note","path":["s-legend"],"text":"[3] Events must follow rule 3.2 #10 for all WSDC Champion J&Js (i.e., they must allow competitors who qualify for Champions based on the WSDC Skill Level Jack and Jill Advancement Chart to compete)."},{"status":"added","key":"3.1.6d","t":"item","path":["3","3.1"],"text":"For petitions down only (in either primary or secondary role):"},{"status":"added","key":"3.1.6e","t":"item","path":["3","3.1"],"text":"NEW! For petitions up only [2] :"},{"status":"added","key":"3.1.6e-i","t":"item","path":["3","3.1"],"text":"Petitions must be submitted to the WSDC Chief Judges Committee (“CJC”) at least fifteen (15) days in advance of the event, along with two (2) videos of the competitor’s dancing. Petitions and videos must be submitted via this link: worldsdc.com/level-up-petition . The CJC may approve or deny the petition after reviewing the competitor’s Points Registry record and videos."},{"status":"added","key":"3.1.6e-ii","t":"item","path":["3","3.1"],"text":"Petitions will be approved for six (6) months and are transferrable to other events. Competitors who obtain a point in the higher division will remain in the higher division."},{"status":"added","key":"3.1.7a","t":"item","path":["3","3.1"],"text":"Competitors are not permitted to dance “down” in a lower skill level contest if the division that they qualify for is not offered (e.g., Advanced dancer may not compete in an Intermediate contest if an Advanced contest is not offered at the event; Champion dancer may not dance in an All Star contest if a Champion contest is not offered)."},{"status":"added","key":"3.2.10","t":"item","path":["3","3.2"],"text":"NEW! For WSDC Champion Jack and Jill contests, competitors may compete (“are allowed”) if they have 1 Champion point or 150 All Star points and must compete (“are required”) if they have 10 Champion points or 225 All Star points, assuming the event offers a WSDC Champion Jack and Jill contest."},{"status":"added","key":"3.2.10b","t":"item","path":["3","3.2"],"text":"Competitors with 10+ Champion points and/or 225+ All Star points (“are required” to compete in Champions) may not enter All Star contests without an approved petition (see Section 3.1 #6 ). Events may offer a combined All Star / Champion contest (see Section 3.1 #7 )."},{"status":"added","key":"legend-2","t":"note","path":["s-legend"],"text":"[2] The new process for petitioning “up” is effective July 1, 2024."},{"status":"added","key":"legend-3","t":"note","path":["s-legend"],"text":"[3] The WSDC announces this interim definition for WSDC Champion divisions, effective July 1, 2024 – June 30, 2025, with the intention to gather additional input for a review by the WSDC Board by June 30, 2025. July 1 – December 31, 2024 will be a transition period. Registry Events that (a) occur during this transition period and (b) have published their Champion definition for their WSDC Champion Jack and Jill publicly prior to May 20, 2024 must obtain approval to maintain their previously published definition by the WSDC Board. Events that have not yet published their Champion definition for WSDC Champion Jack and Jill prior to May 20, 2024 or who do not receive Board approval for a variation must follow the definition listed in Section 3.2 #10 ."},{"status":"added","key":"legend-5","t":"note","path":["s-legend"],"text":"[5] Events must follow rule 3.2 #10 for all WSDC Champion J&Js. See footnote for 3.2 #10 for additional details regarding the transition timeframe."}]}